  nonce: 5d3e  # 5d3e
  message: "Fixed in PR #369 (dev 53de4d2705), Wave-3 Phase-2 §C vocab F6. slice.py and ranking.py hardcoded a structural set {extends, implements} omitting the registered 'inherits' edge type. Added edge_types.INHERITANCE_EDGE_TYPES = frozenset({extends, inherits, implements}) (all AXIS_RELATIONSHIP); slice unions {contains}, ranking uses it directly. find_axis_drift linter validates registry coherence. Method-level 'overrides' deliberately excluded (distinct method->parent relationship neither consumer treated as structural — the item's fix-sketch 'call edge_types_on_axis' would have over-included all 27 relationship-axis types, so a named registered subset is the correct shape). Behavioral evidence (production-path tests on merged dev): test_slice.py::test_forward_slice_skips_inherits_edge (forward slice from a contract that inherits a parent no longer reaches the parent, like extends); test_ranking.py::test_preserves_inherits_edges_from_tests (an inherits edge from a test file now survives filter_edges_for_ranking — was dropped); test_edge_types.py::test_inheritance_edge_types_are_registered_is_a_relationships. 6179 passed, 100% coverage. Confirmed on merged dev: INHERITANCE_EDGE_TYPES = ['extends','implements','inherits']. No bakeoff tag (deterministic behavior verified by tests; inherits edges are rare/Solidity)."  # 5d3e
